CineSphere Deployment Guide (AWS EC2 + Apache + MySQL + PHP)
Step 1: Create EC2 Instance
Ubuntu 26.04 LTS
t2.micro (or higher)
Allow Security Group Ports:
SSH (22)
HTTP (80)
HTTPS (443)

Connect to the instance:

ssh -i "your-key.pem" ubuntu@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP
Step 2: Update Ubuntu
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Step 3: Install Apache
sudo apt install apache2 -y

Start Apache

sudo systemctl start apache2

Enable Apache on boot

sudo systemctl enable apache2

Check status

sudo systemctl status apache2

Restart Apache

sudo systemctl restart apache2

Test

curl http://localhost
Step 4: Install PHP
sudo apt install php php-mysql php-curl php-cli php-json -y

Check version

php -v
Step 5: Install MySQL
sudo apt install mysql-server -y

Start MySQL

sudo systemctl start mysql

Enable MySQL

sudo systemctl enable mysql
Step 6: Login to MySQL
sudo mysql
Step 7: Create Database
CREATE DATABASE cinesphere_db;
Step 8: Create Database User
CREATE USER 'movieuser'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '1234';
Step 9: Give Permissions
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON cinesphere_db.* TO 'movieuser'@'localhost';

FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
Step 10: Exit MySQL
EXIT;
Step 11: Install Git
sudo apt install git -y
Step 12: Go to Apache Folder
cd /var/www/html

Delete default page

sudo rm -f index.html
Step 13: Clone GitHub Repository
sudo git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git

Example

sudo git clone https://github.com/VigneshwaranT/CineSphere.git
Step 14: Copy Project Files
sudo cp -r /var/www/html/CineSphere/* /var/www/html/
Step 15: Set Permissions
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html

sudo chmod -R 755 /var/www/html
Step 16: Import Database
cd /var/www/html

mysql -u movieuser -p cinesphere_db < database.sql

Password

1234
Step 17: Configure Database

Open

sudo nano /var/www/html/backend/db.php

or

sudo nano /var/www/html/backend/config.php

Use

$host="localhost";
$db="cinesphere_db";
$user="movieuser";
$pass="1234";

Save

Ctrl + O

Enter

Ctrl + X
Step 18: Configure TMDB API

Open

sudo nano /var/www/html/backend/tmdb_config.php

Replace

define('TMDB_API_KEY','YOUR_TMDB_API_KEY_HERE');

with

define('TMDB_API_KEY','YOUR_API_KEY');

Save

Ctrl+O

Enter

Ctrl+X
Step 19: Restart Apache
sudo systemctl restart apache2
Step 20: Check Apache
sudo systemctl status apache2

Should show

active (running)
Step 21: Test Database
php /var/www/html/backenddb.php

Expected

DB CONNECTED SUCCESSFULLY
Step 22: Test Website

Local

curl http://localhost

Public

http://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

Example

http://13.203.xxx.xxx
Step 23: Check API

Movies API

http://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP/backend/movies.php?action=all

Expected

[
 {
   "title":"Spider-Man",
   ...
 }
]
Step 24: Useful Commands

Restart Apache

sudo systemctl restart apache2

Start Apache

sudo systemctl start apache2

Stop Apache

sudo systemctl stop apache2

Apache Status

sudo systemctl status apache2

Restart MySQL

sudo systemctl restart mysql

MySQL Status

sudo systemctl status mysql
Step 25: Git Update (Later)
cd /var/www/html/CineSphere

sudo git pull

Copy updated files

sudo cp -r /var/www/html/CineSphere/* /var/www/html/

Restart Apache

sudo systemctl restart apache2
Step 26: Common Errors
Website not opening
sudo systemctl status apache2
Database not connecting
php /var/www/html/backenddb.php
API not loading
curl http://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP/backend/movies.php?action=all
Check Apache Logs
sudo tail -100 /var/log/apache2/error.log
Check PHP Modules
php -m
Check MySQL
sudo mysql
Check Public IP
curl ifconfig.me
Check Local IP
hostname -I
Check Port 80
sudo ss -tlnp | grep :80
Verify Apache Virtual Host
sudo apache2ctl -S
